      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 1986 John Wiley & Sons, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "A direct minimization method previously presented by the authors is applied here to biconfigurational wave functions. A very moderate increasing in the time by iteration with respect to the one-determinant calculation and good convergence properties have been found. So qualitatively correct studies on singlet systems with strong biradical character can be performed with a cost similar to that required by Hartree-Fock calculations."
      },
